pySMESH: SMESH_subMesh checks the algorithm again when a hypothesis is removed from a sub-mesh
that misses one (SMESH V9_16_0).

Defect: a sub-mesh whose algorithm refused its hypotheses stays unmeshable after the hypothesis
that made it refuse is removed. The compute then leaves it empty and reports no error.

Symptom: the unit box with Regular_1D (4 segments), Quadrangle_2D, Hexa_3D and two
ViscousLayers hypotheses on the compound root, one on the face x = 0 and one on x = 1. Hexa_3D
takes one ViscousLayers (StdMeshers_Hexa_3D.cxx:136-147), so the SOLID's sub-mesh becomes
MISSING_HYP. With either hypothesis removed, Hexa_3D accepts the one left, but the SOLID stays
MISSING_HYP and SMESH_Gen::Compute meshes no volume there and returns true.

Root cause: SMESH_subMesh::AlgoStateEngine, state MISSING_HYP, does nothing on REMOVE_HYP
(SMESH_subMesh.cxx:818-819) and on REMOVE_FATHER_HYP (":856-857, nothing to do"); it assumes
that removing a hypothesis cannot make the algorithm's check pass. The HYP_OK state checks again
on REMOVE_HYP (:929-936), and MISSING_HYP checks again on MODIF_HYP and ADD_FATHER_HYP
(:835-844). The removal branches are from SMESH bc37f0b49 (2004-06-18, "DCQ : Merge with
Ecole_Ete_a6"); upstream master at 83f8bf482 (2026-09-14) has the same code.

Change, in SMESH_subMesh.cxx only: in the MISSING_HYP state, REMOVE_HYP and REMOVE_FATHER_HYP
call the algorithm's CheckHypothesis, and the sub-mesh becomes HYP_OK if it passes, as on
ADD_FATHER_HYP.

Not changed: a sub-mesh in any other state; a MISSING_HYP sub-mesh whose algorithm still
refuses its hypotheses after the removal; the status that the removal returns.

diff --git a/src/SMESH/SMESH_subMesh.cxx b/src/SMESH/SMESH_subMesh.cxx
--- a/src/SMESH/SMESH_subMesh.cxx
+++ b/src/SMESH/SMESH_subMesh.cxx
@@ -816,7 +816,16 @@
       break;
     }
     case REMOVE_HYP:
-      break;
+    case REMOVE_FATHER_HYP: {
+      // pySMESH: a removed hypothesis can be what made the algorithm refuse the others
+      // (Hexa_3D takes one ViscousLayers, and a second one makes it HYP_INCOMPATIBLE), so
+      // check again, as MODIF_HYP and ADD_FATHER_HYP do. The sub-mesh stayed MISSING_HYP.
+      algo = GetAlgo();
+      ASSERT(algo);
+      if ( algo->CheckHypothesis((*_father),_subShape, aux_ret ))
+        setAlgoState(HYP_OK);
+      break;
+    }
     case REMOVE_ALGO: {        // perhaps a father algo applies ?
       algo = GetAlgo();
       if (algo == NULL)  // no more algo applying on sub-shape...
@@ -853,8 +862,6 @@
       }
       break;
     }
-    case REMOVE_FATHER_HYP:    // nothing to do
-      break;
     case REMOVE_FATHER_ALGO: {
       algo = GetAlgo();
       if (algo == NULL)  // no more applying algo on father
